components.responsibility:
Creates two tables and one index. It alters nothing in users, sessions, reports or votes.

(1) `comments` (STRICT):
- id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT;
- report_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES reports(id) ON DELETE CASCADE;
- parent_id INTEGER (NULL = top level);
- github_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES users(github_id), with no ON DELETE action, so NO ACTION;
- body TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (length(body) > 0);
- created_at INTEGER NOT NULL (unix seconds);
- removed_at INTEGER (NULL = not removed; SC-020 sets it);
- UNIQUE (report_id, id);
- FOREIGN KEY (report_id, parent_id) REFERENCES comments(report_id, id), with no ON DELETE action, so NO ACTION.

(2) `blocked_accounts` (STRICT): github_id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY CHECK (github_id > 0), blocked_at INTEGER NOT NULL. It has no FK to users, so an account can be blocked before it ever signs in. SC-021 writes it; a row means blocked, and unblocking deletes the row.

(3) `CREATE INDEX comments_children ON comments(report_id, parent_id)`, the child-key index of the self-FK.

There is no owner, role or badge column, and no copied login or avatar. The file header comment states the invariants.

The three architecture_rules of this design land under '# settled by SL-006':
- comments SQL only in internal/comments;
- no transaction in internal/comments;
- no ViewerFrom in internal/server/comment.go.

Each `because` names its known holes the way the votes rules do (lower-case SQL, a table name built by concatenation, quoted or schema-qualified names) and stops there (lesson #939). internal/fitnessrules/testdata/rule_spellings.json lists the three names in `rules`, with at least one fire row and one quiet row each. The quiet rows include `FROM blocked_accounts` and a prose string holding the lower-case word comments.

key_decisions.decision:
Schema 0004:
- one adjacency-list `comments` table with an AUTOINCREMENT id;
- report_id CASCADE from reports;
- a composite parent FK (report_id, parent_id) → comments(report_id, id), backed by UNIQUE(report_id, id), with NO ACTION, not CASCADE;
- github_id → users with NO ACTION;
- body CHECK length > 0 only;
- removed_at nullable;
- a separate `blocked_accounts(github_id PK, blocked_at)` with no FK to users.
No stored owner flag, depth, path or descendant counter.

contracts.notes:
Drawn inside the found state only:
- section#comments with h2 'Comments';
- each kept comment is article#comment-<id>;
- a visible comment's own part: avatar img (only when avatar_url is non-empty), login, 'Author' badge only for the pinned owner's ID, absolute UTC <time>, and p.body as literal text; a details 'Reply' form when signed in;
- replies nest as DOM descendants through div.replies, two elements per level, capped at threadDepthCap;
- a placeholder shows 'Comment removed', keeps its id and keeps its kept replies nested inside.
The bytes are the same on / and /reports/<newest> for any one viewer. No number sits beside the word comment(s), and the word 'author' appears only in the badge.

epic_parts.builds:
Of this design it builds:
- threadDepthCap lowered from 100 to 5 in internal/server/thread.go;
- the Cut marker in define "comment" replaced by `<a class="continue" href="/reports/{{.Slug}}/comments/{{.ID}}">continue this thread →</a>` inside the cut article;
- the GET /reports/{slug}/comments/{id} contract: internal/server/branch.go and templates/branch.html, reusing comments.Book.Tree, buildThread and define "comment" unchanged, with a link back to /reports/<slug>, reply forms, identical http.NotFound for every unusable id, and no iframe;
- comments.Book.Ancestry (one WITH RECURSIVE read) and postComment's success target: D ≤ 5 goes to /reports/<slug>#comment-<id>; otherwise to /reports/<slug>/comments/<ancestor at depth 5+4·⌊(D−6)/4⌋>#comment-<id>; #comments if the read fails, never a 5xx after a stored write;
- the toggle contract: a button.toggle that is hidden until the script runs, aria-controls=replies-<id>, static/thread.js loaded from report.html and branch.html, and a `[hidden]{display:none!important}` guard in site.css.

Shown by:
- python tests/acceptance/test_e004_2_deep_threads_and_toggle.py: levels 1-5 nested on / and /reports/<slug> and level 6 absent; the continue link inside the depth-5 comment; the branch page shows levels 6-8, takes replies and links back; every page nests at most 5 deep; FOLD in headless Chrome hides and then shows every nested comment; /raw keeps script-src 'none'.
- Go tests run with -run filters that do not match TestReportScriptsNeverRun: TestCommentDepthCapIsFive; TestBranchContinueLinkOnlyOnCutNodes; TestBranchNotFoundIsIdentical (hidden report, unknown id, another report's id, pruned id, non-canonical id); TestReplyRedirectTable for D = 1..14; TestThreadScriptServed; new TestReaderPathVariants rows (GET, HEAD and POST spellings of /reports/x/comments/{id}, with POST giving 405 Allow: GET, HEAD); a branch URL added to TestDislikesDoNotInterfere's reads.
